    <bpmn:process id="W_W1873" name="W1873. Building &amp; Occupancy Permit Compliance Monitoring" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New store construction completion; annual compliance verification; LGU inspection
Frequency: Per new store (~10–15/year); annual compliance check for existing stores
Volume: ~205 locations
Owner: COO
Participants: COO, Store Manager, Regulatory Officer, Contractor, LGU Building Official
Source: workflow W1873 — Building &amp; Occupancy Permit Compliance Monitoring</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1873_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1873_Lane1" name="COO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1873_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1873_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1873_Lane2" name="Regulatory Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1873_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1873_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1873_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1873_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1873_Start5" name="New store construction completion; annual compliance verification; LGU inspection">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1873_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1873_Task6" name="For new stores: COO coordinates building permit and occupancy permit process…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: For new stores: COO coordinates building permit and occupancy permit process: (a) building permit: contractor applies to LGU Building Official with architectural plans, structural plans, electrical plans, plumbing plans, fire safety plans per National Building Code (PD 1096), (b) construction inspections: LGU Building Official inspects at key construction milestones, (c) Certificate of Occupancy: upon completion, LGU Building Official issues occupancy permit after final inspection confirming building is safe for intended use, (d) store cannot open without Certificate of Occupancy — critical path for new store timeline per W702
Responsible (R): COO
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Per W20/W702</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1873_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1873_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1873_Task7" name="For existing stores: annual compliance verification: (a) Regulatory Officer…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: For existing stores: annual compliance verification: (a) Regulatory Officer verifies each store&#x27;s building and occupancy permits are current and on file, (b) if permits require annual renewal (some LGUs): process renewal before deadline, (c) if physical modifications made to store (renovation per W96, expansion): verify building permit obtained for modifications and updated occupancy permit secured, (d) display current permits in store as required by LGU
Responsible (R): Regulatory Officer
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1 day/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1873_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1873_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1873_Task8" name="If LGU conducts building safety inspection: (a) Store Manager coordinates…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: If LGU conducts building safety inspection: (a) Store Manager coordinates inspection access, (b) COO provides building documentation, (c) if violations found: coordinate corrective action within LGU-specified timeline, (d) if corrective action requires physical modification: initiate facility maintenance per W47 or renovation per W96
Responsible (R): Store Manager / COO
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Per inspection</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1873_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1873_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1873_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1873_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-369 (ensure controlled execution — Property Tax, LGU Compliance &amp; Lease Accounting (PA-42.3).) | - operational: corrections
Owner: COO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1873_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1873_Annotation10" targetRef="W1873_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
