    <bpmn:process id="W_W1874" name="W1874. Property Insurance Portfolio Management &amp; Annual Renewal" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual insurance renewal cycle; new property addition; claim event
Frequency: Annual renewal; claims per event
Volume: ~205 properties insured; annual premium ~PHP 50–100M
Owner: Finance (Insurance Administrator)
Participants: Finance, COO, Insurance Broker, Insurance Companies, Legal Counsel
Source: workflow W1874 — Property Insurance Portfolio Management &amp; Annual Renewal</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1874_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1874_Lane1" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1874_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1874_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1874_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1874_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1874_Lane2" name="CFO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1874_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1874_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1874_Start4" name="Annual insurance renewal cycle; new property addition; claim event">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1874_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1874_Task5" name="Annual renewal preparation (90 days before policy expiry): (a) Finance compiles…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual renewal preparation (90 days before policy expiry): (a) Finance compiles property schedule: all 205 locations with building specifications, replacement values, contents values, location details (flood zone, earthquake zone, typhoon exposure), (b) Insurance Broker obtains quotes from 3–5 insurance companies, (c) Finance evaluates: coverage adequacy, premium competitiveness, deductible levels, policy terms and exclusions, insurer financial strength rating, (d) negotiate policy terms: (i) blanket coverage vs. scheduled per-location coverage, (ii) business interruption coverage (rent loss during building repair), (iii) natural catastrophe coverage (typhoon, earthquake, flood — critical in Philippines), (iv) deductible optimization: higher deductible = lower premium but higher retained risk
Responsible (R): Finance / Insurance Broker
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4–6 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1874_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1874_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1874_Task6" name="CFO approves insurance program: (a) total annual premium vs. budget, (b)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: CFO approves insurance program: (a) total annual premium vs. budget, (b) coverage adequacy: are all properties adequately insured to replacement value? (c) deductible levels appropriate for BuildRight&#x27;s risk appetite?, (d) execute policies; Finance pays annual premium
Responsible (R): CFO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1874_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1874_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1874_Task7" name="Ongoing property schedule management: (a) new stores: add to insurance schedule…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Ongoing property schedule management: (a) new stores: add to insurance schedule within 30 days of lease commencement or property acquisition, (b) store closures: remove from schedule upon lease termination, (c) renovations: update replacement value after significant improvements, (d) Finance provides updated property schedule to insurer quarterly
Responsible (R): Finance
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1874_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1874_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1874_Task8" name="Claims management: (a) if property damage event (typhoon, fire, flood): (i)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Claims management: (a) if property damage event (typhoon, fire, flood): (i) Finance notifies insurer within 24 hours, (ii) COO coordinates damage assessment and emergency repairs per W26 (crisis response), (iii) Finance compiles claim documentation: damage photos, repair estimates, inventory loss, business interruption calculation, (iv) negotiate claim settlement with insurer adjuster, (v) Finance processes claim payment and repair reimbursement, (b) track claim history by location for underwriting analysis
Responsible (R): Finance / COO
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1874_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1874_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1874_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1874_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-369 (ensure controlled execution — Property Tax, LGU Compliance &amp; Lease Accounting (PA-42.3).) | - operational: annual insurance-coverage adequacy review vs reconstruction cost; policy schedule reconciled to the ~205-lease portfolio quarterly
Owner: Finance (Insurance Administrator)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1874_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1874_Annotation10" targetRef="W1874_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
