    <bpmn:process id="W_W1877" name="W1877. Property Utility Account Management &amp; Meter Reading Reconciliation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly utility billing cycle; new store utility connection
Frequency: Monthly verification per location
Volume: ~205 locations × 2–3 utility accounts each (electric, water, gas if applicable)
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Finance, Utility Companies (Meralco, Davao Light, VECO, local water districts)
Source: workflow W1877 — Property Utility Account Management &amp; Meter Reading Reconciliation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1877_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1877_Lane1" name="Utility Company">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1877_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1877_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1877_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1877_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1877_Lane3" name="AP Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1877_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1877_Lane4" name="COO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1877_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1877_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1877_Start6" name="Monthly utility billing cycle; new store utility connection">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1877_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1877_Task7" name="Monthly: utility company issues bill to each location: (a) electricity: kWH…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly: utility company issues bill to each location: (a) electricity: kWH consumption × rate + demand charges + VAT + local franchise tax, (b) water: cubic meters × rate + sewerage charge, (c) some locations: natural gas or LPG delivery billing
Responsible (R): Utility Company
Accountable (A): —
Duration: External</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1877_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1877_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1877_Task8" name="Store Manager or Finance verifies utility bill: (a) compare consumption to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Store Manager or Finance verifies utility bill: (a) compare consumption to prior month and same month previous year — flag unusual spikes (&gt; 20% increase without operational explanation), (b) verify meter reading matches actual meter (some utility companies estimate readings; estimated readings can be inaccurate), (c) verify rate applied matches current tariff schedule (DLPC/Meralco rate changes), (d) if discrepancy: dispute with utility company per their dispute process; pay undisputed amount on time to avoid disconnection
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Finance
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 15–30 min/location</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1877_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1877_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1877_Task9" name="Finance processes utility payment: (a) utility bills typically have short…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Finance processes utility payment: (a) utility bills typically have short payment windows (7–15 days) and severe penalties for late payment (disconnection after 2 months), (b) AP Clerk processes utility payments in weekly payment run per W7, (c) Dr. Utilities Expense / Cr. Cash (entity: BuildRight Property Management or Depot per lease terms), (d) IC settlement if Property Management pays and recharges to Depot
Responsible (R): AP Clerk / Finance
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: Per W7</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1877_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1877_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1877_Task10" name="New store utility connection: (a) COO applies for utility connection with…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: New store utility connection: (a) COO applies for utility connection with Building Permit as supporting document, (b) utility company installs meter and activates service, (c) Store Manager verifies meter installation and initial reading, (d) connection costs (deposit, installation fee) processed per W40 (capex if material) or expensed
Responsible (R): COO / Store Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Per W702</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1877_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1877_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1877_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1877_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-369 (ensure controlled execution — Property Tax, LGU Compliance &amp; Lease Accounting (PA-42.3).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1877_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1877_Annotation12" targetRef="W1877_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1877_Flow14" sourceRef="W1877_Start6" targetRef="W1877_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1877_Flow15" sourceRef="W1877_Task7" targetRef="W1877_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1877_Flow16" sourceRef="W1877_Task8" targetRef="W1877_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1877_Flow17" sourceRef="W1877_Task9" targetRef="W1877_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1877_Flow18" sourceRef="W1877_Task10" targetRef="W1877_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1877_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1877_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1877">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1877_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1877_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1877_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1877_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1877_Lane3_di" bpmnElement="W1877_Lane3" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="420" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1877_Lane4_di" bpmnElement="W1877_Lane4" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="590" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1877_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1877_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1877_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1877_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1877_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W1877_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="465" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1877_Task10_di" bpmnElement="W1877_Task10"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="635" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1877_Start6_di" bpmnElement="W1877_Start6"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1877_End11_di" bpmnElement="W1877_End11"><dc:Bounds x="1260" y="657" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1877_Annotation12_di" bpmnElement="W1877_Annotation12"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="800" width="360" height="72" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1877_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W1877_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1877_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1877_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1877_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1877_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="790" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1877_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W1877_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="505" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="675" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1877_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W1877_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="675" /><di:waypoint x="1260" y="675" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1877_Assoc13_di" bpmnElement="W1877_Assoc13"><di:waypoint x="340" y="800" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W5529" name="W5529. Utility, Telecommunications &amp; Site Deposits Paid — Register, Interest Reconciliation, Surety Replacement &amp; Recovery-on-Closure" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: A new utility or telecommunications service connection requiring a deposit (store opening per W16/W702, DC/HQ changes) or a provider deposit-billing notice; the annual deposit-interest credit cycle or a provider tariff change; a store/DC closure or service disconnection (W703/W807/W1857); or the annual deposit-portfolio review
Frequency: Per-connection/per-provider event; annual interest-credit reconciliation; annual portfolio review; per-closure recovery
Volume: ≈ 450–700 active deposits (electricity, water, and telecom/internet accounts across 200 stores, 4 DCs and HQ, plus entity-level deposits); electric-cooperative deposits of PHP 50K–200K per store and Meralco-class commercial deposits of ~1–3 months&#x27; average bill put total locked capital at PHP 10M–40M (the W1877 pain-point canon); ~15–25 deposit opening/closure events/year; ~205 annual interest-credit verifications
Owner: Treasury Manager
Participants: Lease Administrator, Facilities Coordinator, Energy Manager, AP Clerk, Controller, Legal Counsel (guarantee documentation), CFO (surety-replacement decisions), External bank/surety (guarantee issuance via W232/W325), Utility/telecom providers
Source: workflow W5529 — Utility, Telecommunications &amp; Site Deposits Paid — Register, Interest Reconciliation, Surety Replacement &amp; Recovery-on-Closure</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5529_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5529_Lane1" name="Treasury Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5529_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5529_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5529_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5529_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5529_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5529_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5529_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5529_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5529_Start3" name="A new utility or telecommunications service connection requiring a deposit (store opening…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5529_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5529_Task4" name="Deposit register &amp; policy custody">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Deposit register &amp; policy custody: maintain the deposits-paid register per provider account — provider, site, service type, amount, terms, interest entitlement, renewal/expiry dates, and GL account mapping; deposit approvals above PHP 1M require CFO sign-off; reconcile the register to the GL deposits-receivable accounts quarterly within the W636 balance-sheet reconciliation cycle
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 20 min/month register upkeep + quarterly reconciliation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5529_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5529_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5529_Task5" name="Onboarding &amp; adequacy">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Onboarding &amp; adequacy: process connection deposits for new sites and deposit top-ups where consumption growth or tariff escalation drops a deposit below the provider requirement; cross-check adequacy against the consumption data captured per W1877/W1687/W1563 before approving top-up or renegotiation
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager / Facilities Coordinator
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: ~2 hours per opening/top-up event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5529_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5529_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5529_Task6" name="Interest-credit reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Interest-credit reconciliation: verify each distribution-utility and telecom provider&#x27;s annual deposit-interest credit against the register entitlement (EPIRA IRR customer-deposit interest rules for DUs); chase missing or short credits with the provider; post verified credits to GL
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager / AP Clerk
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 15 min per deposit per year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5529_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5529_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5529_Task7" name="Surety-replacement review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Surety-replacement review: annually evaluate replacing cash deposits with bank/surety guarantees where the provider accepts them (issuance routed through the W232 bank-guarantee / W325 corporate-guarantee machinery); CFO decides cash release vs guarantee fee per account
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: ~1 hour per major account per year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5529_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5529_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5529_Task8" name="Recovery-on-closure">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Recovery-on-closure: on disconnection or site closure, obtain final meter billing, offset deposits against final bills, and pursue refunds within the provider SLA; escalate overdue refunds to the provider relationship owner; attach the deposit-recovery checklist to the W703/W807 store-closure and W1857 lease-termination workflows
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager / AP Clerk
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: ~4 hours per closure event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5529_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5529_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5529_Task9" name="Portfolio reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Portfolio reporting: annual deposits-portfolio report to the CFO — locked capital, interest credited vs entitled, guarantee fees avoided/incurred, recovery aging and open disputes; feeds the W326 treasury month-end close and the annual W636 reconciliation evidence pack
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 8 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5529_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5529_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5529_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5529_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-369 (ensure controlled execution — Property Tax, LGU Compliance &amp; Lease Accounting (PA-42.3).) | - operational: deposits above PHP 1M require CFO approval before payment | - operational: quarterly register-to-GL reconciliation with Controller sign-off | - operational: no closure checklist completes with an unresolved deposit-recovery item
Owner: Treasury Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
